Add a kbase (non-DRM) dispatch path to pan_kmod_dev_create().

pan_kmod_dev_create() identifies a device by calling drmGetVersion() and
matching the DRM driver name against a table. kbase is a misc character
device (/dev/mali0), not a DRM node, so drmGetVersion() fails on it and the
function bails before any backend is consulted.

This adds a probe for kbase *before* the DRM path, mirroring how Turnip
special-cases kgsl (/dev/kgsl-3d0) alongside DRM enumeration. The probe is
KBASE_IOCTL_VERSION_CHECK, side-effect free and clean on a non-kbase fd.

pan_kmod_fd_is_kbase() reports the kbase UK interface version through
out-params rather than having this file issue the ioctl, so pan_kmod.c -
generic, driver-agnostic code - needs no kbase UAPI headers. The declaration
lives in pan_kmod_kbase.h, matching how panthor_kmod.h serves the panthor
backend (Mesa builds with -Werror=missing-prototypes, so a visible prototype
is mandatory, not optional).

The `if (!allocator)` default is hoisted above the probe, since the kbase
path needs the allocator too.

VERIFIED: generated from a tree that builds. Mesa 26.3.0-devel (7296f9a),
native x86_64 Linux, meson 1.11.2 / LLVM 18.1.3. `ninja
src/panfrost/lib/kmod/libpankmod_lib.a` succeeds with pan_kmod_kbase.c.o in
the archive.

